WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:05.120
This video goes through the settings of a UM-Codex setup,

00:05.120 --> 00:08.160
one at a time, and what each one means.

00:08.160 --> 00:09.820
First, Folder.

00:09.820 --> 00:10.400
Then, Access.

00:10.400 --> 00:11.340
Then, Codex.

00:11.340 --> 00:14.288
And last, the box that sums it all up.

00:15.488 --> 00:19.268
Press Edit, a small link under a setup's card, to see them.

00:19.268 --> 00:22.028
For a new setup, press New setup instead.

00:22.028 --> 00:27.056
It's all on one page, in three sections, and nothing changes until you press Save.

00:28.256 --> 00:31.776
Under Folder, the working folder is where Codex starts.

00:31.776 --> 00:34.716
It can read, change and delete files there.

00:34.716 --> 00:38.656
They're your real files, with no undo, so use a copy,

00:38.656 --> 00:42.176
or a folder that's a git repository, for anything important.

00:42.176 --> 00:44.600
Change opens your Mac's folder picker.

00:45.100 --> 00:47.040
More folders lets you add others.

00:47.040 --> 00:49.760
Each one is either Read only or Read and write.

00:49.760 --> 00:53.060
Read only means Codex can look but not change,

00:53.060 --> 00:56.080
even with administrator rights inside the sandbox.

00:56.080 --> 00:59.260
Read and write means it can change and delete there too.

01:00.460 --> 01:04.060
Under Access, Internet decides what Codex can reach.

01:04.060 --> 01:05.800
On means the whole internet,

01:05.800 --> 01:10.080
and also programs on this computer and your local network or VPN.

01:10.080 --> 01:15.964
Off means Codex can reach only the model: no downloads, no installs, no websites.

01:16.464 --> 01:19.204
With the internet on, there's a Browser tool.

01:19.204 --> 01:20.944
It's off until you turn it on.

01:20.944 --> 01:25.644
It gives Codex a fresh browser inside the sandbox, with none of your logins.

01:25.644 --> 01:29.244
When it's on, Approve each browser action is on too:

01:29.244 --> 01:33.424
Codex stops and asks before it opens a page, clicks, or types.

01:33.424 --> 01:35.324
Reading a page doesn't ask.

01:35.324 --> 01:40.224
Turn the internet off, and the Browser tool goes away, because it needs the internet.

01:41.424 --> 01:47.584
Under Codex, Model is the model Codex uses, newest first, with the setup's own selected.

01:47.584 --> 01:51.084
A new setup starts on gpt-5.6-terra.

01:51.084 --> 01:54.484
Open in is where Codex opens: in the Codex app,

01:54.484 --> 01:57.336
on a Mac that has it, or in a Terminal window.

01:57.836 --> 02:01.676
Under More options, Ask before commands is off by default:

02:01.676 --> 02:06.056
Codex runs commands without asking, and the sandbox is what keeps it in.

02:06.056 --> 02:08.636
Turn it on, and Codex asks first.

02:08.636 --> 02:12.916
Name is what the card, and the project in the Codex app, are called.

02:12.916 --> 02:16.616
Where Codex runs is In the sandbox, which is recommended.

02:16.616 --> 02:20.736
On this computer is experimental: Codex works directly on your Mac,

02:20.736 --> 02:24.476
with no sandbox around it, so it can do anything you can do there.

02:24.476 --> 02:26.556
It asks you to confirm first.

02:26.556 --> 02:29.108
Leave it on the sandbox unless you need that.

02:30.308 --> 02:36.208
At the bottom, What Codex gets sums up your choices in plain words, and changes as you do.

02:36.208 --> 02:40.468
Your Toolkit key stays on this computer: the sandbox never sees it.

02:40.468 --> 02:43.408
Then press Save and start, or just Save.

02:43.408 --> 02:47.684
If the setup is already running, changes apply the next time it starts.

02:48.184 --> 02:49.524
That's every setting.

02:49.524 --> 02:52.000
You can change any of them later, with Edit.
